  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 8005.02 Issuance of Original License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 8005.02 Issuance of Original License.\n\n(a) An individual applicant who meets the educational and licensing requirements in accordance with these rules and who submits a completed application, pursuant to Saf-C 8005.01, shall be issued a pocket card and wall license.\n\n(b) The individual licensee pocket card, DSFM 126, and wall certificate, DSFM 125, shall contain at minimum the following:\n\n(1) The individual’s name;\n\n(2) The individual’s photo;\n\n(3) The license number;\n\n(4) The type of specialty license;\n\n(5) The date of issuance; and\n\n(6) The expiration date of the license.\n\n(c) The individual licensee wall certificate, DSFM 125, shall contain at minimum the following:\n\n(1) The individual’s name;\n\n(2) The license number;\n\n(3) The type of specialty license;\n\n(4) The date of issuance; and\n\n(5) The expiration date of the license.\n\n(d) All individual licenses issued shall expire on the last day of the month of the applicant’s birthday, 2 years from the date of issuance.\n\n(e) A business entity that meets the licensing requirements in accordance with these rules and who submits a completed application pursuant to Saf-C 8005.01(c), shall be issued a wall certificate.\n\n(f) The business entity wall certificate shall contain at minimum the following:\n\n(1) The business entity’s name;\n\n(2) The business entity’s license number;\n\n(3) The responsible managing employee’s name;\n\n(4) The responsible managing employee’s license number;\n\n(5) The expiration date of the responsible managing employee’s license number; and\n\n(6) The expiration date of the business entity’s license number.\n\n(g) All business entity licenses shall expire on the last day of December in each 2-year period.\n\nSource. #8954, eff 7-21-07; ss by #9542, eff 9-10-09",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c8000.html"
